  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Weather will be fair yet cool across the\nforecast area today and tonight with high level clouds increasing\nfrom the west. Daytime high temperatures will be in the low 50s to\nlow 60s with overnight lows in the low 20s to low 30s. \n\nA modest Pacific low pressure system moving into the PacNW early\nMonday morning will drag a weak cold front thru Northern Nevada\nfrom the west-northwest during the day Monday. This will produce\nisolated light valley rain showers and mountain show showers\nacross much of northern Nevada, though the best chance for any \nactivity will be north of the I-80 corridor. Significant\naccumulation is not expected under any showers with a tenth of an\ninch or less forecast. West-southwesterly winds will also become \nbreezy Monday with widespread gusts 30 to 35 mph. Winds shift \nwest-northwesterly Monday night while concurrently easing. \n\nGenerally zonal flow will be present over Nevada beginning\nTuesday, eventually shifting to southwesterly by Thursday as a\ndeep upper level trof takes shape off the coast of the western\nU.S. Weather thru mid week will be generally fair yet cool,\nresiding near to a few degrees cooler than seasonal. Light winds\non Tuesday will gradually increase each day thru Thursday in\nresponse to the deepening upper level trof offshore. By the\nThursday night/Friday time frame, numerical model solutions depict\nthe beginning of a period of unsettled weather, including\nincreasing probabilities of precipitation thru the weekend as \nwell as breezes. Model solutions depict the upper level trof \nprogressing thru Nevada from the west Sunday/Sunday night.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Moderate forecast confidence in\nthe possibility of valley rain and mountain snow across Northern \nNevada Monday thru Monday night. Low forecast confidence\npertaining to active weather at the end of the week and next\nweekend. Utilized various model blends for PoP and weather fields.",
